cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Synesyn
message: >-
  If you use Synesyn in academic or artistic research, please cite both the
  software and the research project it comes out of.
type: software
abstract: >-
  A local-first, artifact-centric platform for groups to reason with AI about
  possible futures, drawing them out of material they already hold and building up
  a traceable record from one session to the next. Everything a session produces is
  stored as a versioned artifact with provenance, so any result can be traced back
  to the inputs, models and human decisions that produced it.
authors:
  - given-names: Ayodele
    family-names: Arigbabu
    affiliation: Trondheim Academy of Fine Art, NTNU
repository-code: "https://github.com/Metapunkt/Synesyn"
url: "https://www.metapunkt.org/"
license: MIT
# 0.1.0 is the first public release. Add date-released when it is tagged.
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - speculative design
  - strategic foresight
  - artistic research
  - generative theatre
  - human-AI collaboration
  - provenance
  - Godot
references:
  - type: generic
    title: "Forward Remembrance: Exploring Latent Utopias"
    abstract: >-
      The artistic PhD research project this software was built to make operable.
    authors:
      - given-names: Ayodele
        family-names: Arigbabu
    institution:
      name: Trondheim Academy of Fine Art, Norwegian University of Science and Technology (NTNU)
